# Troubleshooter

Internal HRMS data/access operator console (`apps/troubleshooter`, port 5100). Next.js 16 App Router + React 19 + Ant Design 6 + Tailwind 4. Full layout is in `apps/troubleshooter/AGENTS.md`.

Do **not** import `@hrms/ui`. Components are `antd` only. Icons are `@ant-design/icons` only.

## Feature folders

`src/app/` is a thin route map. Feature code is `src/features/<domain>/<capability>/` with a leaf `index.ts`. Domain folders are singular. Do not prefix the capability with the domain.

```text
# ❌ BAD
features/employee-access/employee-access-screen.tsx
features/employer-settings/
features/roles/

# ✅ GOOD
features/employee/access/access-screen.tsx
features/employer/settings/settings-screen.tsx
features/employer/roles/roles-screen.tsx
```

- No domain-level barrel. Import `@/features/employee/access`, not `@/features/employee`.
- Same capability on two domains = two folders (`employer/roles` vs future `employee/roles`).
- App-wide login stays `features/auth/`. Cross-cutting resolve stays `shared/employee/`.
- URL routes stay nested under `/employers/[id]/...`. Do not flatten features to match URLs.

Import with `@/`. No parent-relative `../`. Same-directory `./` is allowed.

## Server Components

- Do not use dotted Ant Design subcomponents (`Typography.Title`). Import `Title` / `Text` / `Paragraph` from `@/shared/ui` or `antd/es/...`.
- Pass a serializable `items` array to `Descriptions`. Do not use `Descriptions.Item` children.
- Do not pass `render` (or other functions) in Table `columns` from a Server Component. Put the table in a `"use client"` file.
- Use Alert `title`, not deprecated `message`.

## Data and writes

Queries go through `@hrms/db`. Do not use `mssql` or raw SQL strings. Do not call HRMS stored procedures (`SP_AdminRoleM_*`, `SP_InsertRolePageMapping`, `sp_InsertDynamicMenuHierarchy`).

Every query includes `Employerid`. Writes require `TROUBLESHOOTER_WRITES_ENABLED=1`, non-production `NODE_ENV`, and the selected env in `TROUBLESHOOTER_WRITES_ENVS`. Preview → HMAC confirm → `BEGIN TRAN` / `COMMIT`.
